ids_shared.txt -- the cross-arm population. 10,421 question ids, sha256 (sorted, comma
joined, first 16 hex) = cae4daf7ad59388c. Every accepted row in this directory reports
this same sha, and eval_heldout.py REFUSES to score if a requested id does not fit the arm.

Built as the INTERSECTION of the two arms keep-sets, each computed at the seq that arm
TRAINED at: ours 10,613 at seq 4096 (sha 433e835a7859c63e), control 10,421 at seq 2048
(sha cae4daf7ad59388c). The control set is a strict subset here, so the intersection equals
it -- that is a property of these two seqs and this data, NOT a guarantee, which is why the
criterion is "both arms report the same evaluated_ids_sha256" and not "the control set is
smaller".

COPIED HERE FROM /tmp/e1_scratch/ ON 2026-09-03Z. It was generated in /tmp, which does not
survive a container restart -- and this file is what defines the population every number in
this directory is computed over. The numbers would remain in the JSONs but nothing could be
recomputed on the same set. Keeping the population next to the results it defines.
